      "pmid": "36338980",
      "pmcid": "PMC9634069",
      "doi": "10.3389/fgene.2022.1034947",
      "title": "Identification of genomic regions of wheat associated with grain Fe and Zn content under drought and heat stress using genome-wide association study.",
      "authorString": "Devate NB, Krishna H, Sunilkumar VP, Manjunath KK, Mishra CN, Jain N, Singh GP, Singh PK.",
      "journalTitle": "Frontiers in genetics",
      "pubYear": 2022,
      "firstPublicationDate": "2022-10-21",
      "citedByCount": 11,
      "isOpenAccess": true,
      "hasPDF": true,
      "abstractText": "Wheat is the staple food crop of global importance for its grain nutrient quality. Grain iron and zinc content of the wheat grain is an important quantitatively inherited trait that is influenced by the environmental factors such as drought and heat stress. Phenotypic evaluation of 295 advanced breeding lines from the wheat stress breeding program of IARI was carried out under timely sown irrigated (IR), restricted irrigated, and late-sown conditions at New Delhi during the cropping season of 2020-21, and grain iron (GFeC) and zinc (GZnC) contents were estimated from both control and treatments. A statistically significant increase in GFeC and GZnC was observed under stress conditions compared to that of the control. Genotyping was carried out with the SNPs from the 35K Axiom Breeder's array, and marker-trait association was identified by GWAS analysis. Of the 23 MTAs identified, seven were linked with GFeC and sixteen were linked with GZnC. <i>In silico</i> analysis revealed a few important transcripts involved in various plant metabolism, growth, and development activities such as <i>auxin response factor</i>, <i>root UVB sensitive proteins</i>, <i>potassium transporter</i>, <i>glycosyl transferase</i>, <i>COBRA</i>, and <i>F-box-like domain.</i> The identified MTAs can be used for molecular breeding after validation and also for rapid development of micronutrient-rich varieties of wheat to mitigate hidden hunger.",
      "web_url": "https://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC9634069"
     }
    ],
